{
  "_comment": "A BENIGN line long enough to prove the parse fits its budget. `hooks.json` gives this gate 5s and the selftest harness kills a leg at 30s; a hook killed at its budget writes no stdout, and the harness reads that as ALLOW, so a slow parse is a bypass with a stopwatch and the harness timeout is what turns time into a verdict. Every token here is an OPAQUE head, which is the shape that made three separate quadratics bite at once: `_peel_candidates` built and joined a tail LIST per token, `_api_write_action` ran a 1.7ms regex per synthesized `curl` candidate, and `_alias_definition_form` ran two lazy `[^|&;]*?` regexes per candidate. 12000 tokens, not 8000, because at 8000 every reverted fix still finished inside the 30s harness timeout (18.4s and 16.8s) and the leg passed anyway: 12000 is 1.6s fixed against 49.1s and 52.4s reverted. It is the only fixture in this set that proves a timing property.",
